    "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 2623 reported a net release of $150.8 million in prior year reserves for 2021. This was primarily driven by sizeable claims releases across the 2019 underwriting year, particularly in Marine, Property, Reinsurance, and Specialty lines. The Property division also benefited from a $40.8 million release due to a Loss Portfolio Transfer (LPT) for Engineering classes. These releases occurred despite adverse impacts from the COVID-19 pandemic, natural catastrophes (Hurricanes Laura, Sally, Delta, Zeta, Storm Dorian, Typhoons Faxai, Hagibis), and an increase in ransomware claims activity on the 2020 underwriting year, which led to strengthening in Political, Accident & Contingency reserves.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "released prior year reserves of $150.8m",
      "adversely impacted by some large claims attributable to the COVID-19 pandemic and natural catastrophes such as Hurricanes Laura, Sally, Delta and Zeta, Storm Dorian and Typhoons Faxai and Hagibis",
      "culminating in sizeable claims releases across the 2019 underwriting year",
      "Cyber & Executive Risk produced a net release of $20.2m despite an increase in ransomware claims activity on the 2020 underwriting year",
      "entering into a 90% Loss Portfolio Transfer (LPT) of the divisions Engineering classes in March 2021, contributing to the release of $40.8m in the division"
